; Module-definition file for MosaicThumbnail.dll -- the .mosaic IThumbnailProvider shell extension
; (src/thumbnailer/shell_thumbnail_win32.cpp, PLAN.md S57). This file is the ONLY thing that gives
; the DLL an export table, and it does two jobs that a shell extension cannot do without:
;
;   1. It exports the four COM entry points the shell and regsvr32 look up BY NAME. There is no
;      __declspec(dllexport) in the .cpp on purpose -- <combaseapi.h> pre-declares two of these four
;      without the attribute, so adding it there is an error on the clang/aarch64 toolchain, while
;      GCC accepts it. Naming them here works identically on both.
;   2. It SUPPRESSES the auto-export fallback. Handed a DLL with no explicit exports, GNU ld exports
;      every global symbol in the image -- which, for a module that statically links mosaic_io, means
;      publishing a table full of Mosaic internals to anything that cares to look.
;
; No LIBRARY statement: the internal module name then follows the real output file name, so renaming
; the target in CMakeLists.txt cannot leave a stale name embedded in the PE export directory. No
; ordinals either -- COM resolves these by name, always, and an ordinal would be one more thing that
; has to stay in step with nothing.
EXPORTS
    DllGetClassObject
    DllCanUnloadNow
    DllRegisterServer
    DllUnregisterServer
